ry what we are doing for  infant  in this country is abysmal it is a  disgrace it is criminal we have child  care workers all over this country who  are earning six or seven dollars an hour  who do not have benefits who do not have  chaining children at the most vulnerable  age of their lives are not getting the  proper nutrition are not getting the cup  of proper nurturing that they need and  these are the kids who are now becoming  more violent who will do worse in school  who will end up in jail so instead of  investing in tax breaks for billionaires  it seems to me a lot more sensible that  we provide significant increases in  child care funding years ago the United  States Congress made a pledge to school  systems all over this country and it  said that if you mainstream children  with disabilities we will provide forty  percent of the funding meanwhile in  Vermont and in school districts all over  America school systems are struggling  because they have in fact mainstream  their kids which is an expensive  proposition but the federal government  has in no way kept its commitment in  terms of that forty percent of funding  to we ignore those realities of higher  education of child care of special  education of a dozen other areas in  education and saying we think a more  important priority as tax breaks for  billionaires is absolutely immoral and  absurd and I can tell you that the  Progressive Caucus is going to fight  this tooth nail we're going to go to the  American people and we're going to stop  these outrageous tax breaks for people  who don't need them
 

